<title>MEXICO: Mexican states lobbying for natural gas duct.</title>
<headline>Mexican states lobbying for natural gas duct.</headline>
<dateline>GUADALAJARA, Mexico 1997-01-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican state governors are lobbying the Energy Ministry to construct a natural gas duct connecting principal cities in Western Mexico, the Jalisco government said in a press statement Tuesday.</p>
<p>The duct would extend between Mexico's second largest city, Guadalajara in Jalisco, and the nation's second busiest port, Manzanillo in Colima state, and run 257 kilometers (about 160 miles).</p>
<p>State officials said a group of Texan investors have expressed interest in partly financing the gas duct.</p>
<p>((--Monica Ballesca, Guadalajara bureau +913 817-0397))</p>
